/-!
# Smoothing a local complete intersection essentially of finite type over a field

A local `k`-algebra `A` essentially of finite type over a field `k` and a complete intersection
over `k` is the special fibre `B/tB` of a flat `k⟦t⟧`-algebra `B` essentially of finite type over
`k⟦t⟧`, for which some power `t^n` lies in the `d`-th Fitting ideal of `Ω_{B/k⟦t⟧}`, where
`d = dim(A) + trdeg_k(κ)` and `κ` is the residue field of `A`.

The witness is produced from the smoothing of a global complete intersection: `A` is a
localization `P_𝔭` of a global complete intersection `P` over `k` at a prime, the dimension
formula for a finite type algebra over a field identifies `dim(P)` with `d`, the smoothing of `P`
is a flat finite type `k⟦t⟧`-algebra `Q` with `Q/tQ ≅ P` carrying a relative global complete
intersection presentation of relative dimension `d` and with smooth generic fibre, and `B` is the
localization of `Q` at the prime of `Q` corresponding to the closed point of `P_𝔭`. Smoothness of
the generic fibre makes the `d`-th Fitting ideal of its differentials the unit ideal, because over
a smooth algebra of dimension at most `d` the relative cotangent space at every prime is generated
by `d` elements; since the generic fibre is the localization of `Q` at the powers of `t`, and
Fitting ideals commute with that localization, a power of `t` already lies in the `d`-th Fitting
ideal over `Q`, hence over `B`.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.Smoothing.exists_flat_essFiniteType_specialFiber_pow_mem_fittingIdeal`:
  the smoothing of a local complete intersection essentially of finite type over a field, together
  with the Fitting ideal membership.

## Implementation notes

The two numbers `dim(A)` and `trdeg_k(κ)` are returned as natural numbers whose casts are the
Krull dimension and the transcendence degree; both are finite because `A` is a Noetherian local
ring essentially of finite type over `k`. The special fibre `B/tB` is the quotient of `B` by the
ideal generated by the image of `PowerSeries.X`, and the generic fibre is the base change along
`k⟦t⟧ → k⸨t⸩`.

The base field is lifted to `ULift k` in the course of the proof. The source's `P` is a global
complete intersection over `k` of which `A` is a localization at a prime, so `P` must be large
enough to carry the given `A`, while the criterion that produces it quantifies `P` in the universe
of the base field; replacing `k` by `ULift k` makes those two universes agree, and the
transcendence degree of the residue field is unchanged because `ULift k → k` is an algebraic
extension.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E7X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E7X)
